{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"JLSEC-2026-990","published":"2026-07-30T16:02:27.435Z","modified":"2026-07-30T18:35:32.491551914Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-32636","EUVD-2026-12962","GHSA-gc62-2v5p-qpmp"],"summary":"ImageMagick has a heap-buffer-overflow in NewXMLTree which could result in crash","details":"ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. Prior to 7.1.2-17 and 6.9.13-42, the NewXMLTree method contains a bug that could result in a crash due to an out of write bounds of a single zero byte. Versions 7.1.2-17 and 6.9.13-42 fix the issue.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"ImageMagick_jll","ecosystem":"Julia","purl":"pkg:julia/ImageMagick_jll?uuid=c73af94c-d91f-53ed-93a7-00f77d67a9d7"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.1.2023+0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/SecurityAdvisories.jl/tree/generated/osv/2026/JLSEC-2026-990.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/releases/tag/7.1.2-17"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-gc62-2v5p-qpmp"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gc62-2v5p-qpmp"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/dlemstra/Magick.NET/releases/tag/14.11.0"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-32636"}],"database_specific":{"license":"CC-BY-4.0","sources":[{"database_specific":{"status":"Analyzed"},"html_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-32636","id":"CVE-2026-32636","imported":"2026-07-30T14:08:46.462Z","modified":"2026-06-17T10:36:08.627Z","published":"2026-03-18T21:16:26.583Z","url":"https://services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cves/2.0?cveId=CVE-2026-32636"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gc62-2v5p-qpmp","id":"GHSA-gc62-2v5p-qpmp","imported":"2026-07-30T14:10:16.714Z","modified":"2026-03-18T21:51:15Z","published":"2026-03-17T17:12:34Z","url":"https://api.github.com/adv